It's about 40 lines, and owning it beats importing it:

for _ in range(MAX_STEPS):
  resp = client.messages.create(model=MODEL, messages=msgs, tools=TOOLS)
  msgs.append({'role': 'assistant', 'content': resp.content})   # the forgotten line
  if resp.stop_reason == 'tool_use':
    results = []
    for block in resp.content:
      if block.type == 'tool_use':
        args = validate(block.name, block.input)   # Pydantic, before execution
        results.append(tool_result(block.id, execute(block.name, args)))
    msgs.append({'role': 'user', 'content': results})
  else:
    return extract_text(resp)
raise AgentBudgetExceeded(transcript=msgs)

Guards that make it production-shaped: MAX_STEPS and a per-run cost cap; argument validation before execution; a tool allowlist per task; repeated-identical-call detection; and the full transcript logged, because the transcript IS the debugging artifact - and the state, if you want resumability.
